    "done_when": "reckon/_store.py gains write_json_atomically beside its existing envelope writer. It writes a unique sibling temporary file, removes it on any failure, and takes an fsync parameter that defaults on. It reuses the envelope writer's own rename step rather than copying it. A new module reckon/_observations.py provides optional_number, which rejects a bool and any value that is not an int or a float, and otherwise returns float(value). No caller is migrated in this node. Instead, the manifest lists the fourteen atomic-JSON writers and the four numeric-decoder bodies at main HEAD, as file:symbol found with git grep, each with the fsync behaviour and locking it has today that its migration must keep. tests/test_one_atomic_writer_and_number_decoder.py covers four behaviours: the writer leaves no temporary file behind after a failure it injects; two concurrent writers never interleave; fsync is called when on and not when off; and optional_number returns None for True, False, a string, None and a list, and a float for an int and a float. It passes at exit 0, as does the existing store test file. The manifest records base and head arms in the armed JSON form with FAILED ids, and the head arm is run at the committed head. The declared negative control is applied, the no-stray-temporary case is observed to fail, and that log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED test id.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Add the one atomic JSON writer and the one numeric decoder that their duplicated copies will migrate to",
